WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.630
An eligible Prime free trial can give you time to compare purchases before Prime Day. It does not guarantee discounts, stock, or trial eligibility.

2
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:20.380
Start with the official sale dates. Summer Prime Day and autumn Prime Big Deal Days are separate events. Do not schedule a trial around a guessed date.

3
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:29.570
Read the trial length, renewal date, and price shown on your account. If the page charges you today, do not assume the offer is free.

4
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:38.620
Choose a start date that leaves preparation time and keeps the full sale inside your offered trial. Set a reminder several days before renewal.

5
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:50.410
Write down the exact products you need and the most you will pay. Compare final prices, delivery, accessories, and return terms. A discount badge is not proof of value.

6
00:00:50.410 --> 00:01:01.580
Test delivery at your actual address and entertainment you would really use. Rentals, add-on channels, Audible, and Kindle Unlimited can involve separate charges.

7
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:14.000
Before renewal, review actual benefits and extra spending. Check discounted Prime options if you may qualify. If you cancel, save the confirmation and verify when benefits end.

8
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:26.840
